WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:03.774
- In this video, we're gonna talk about

00:00:03.774 --> 00:00:05.107
how to burn fat,

00:00:07.688 --> 00:00:10.436
a very important topic,

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:13.678
but a big problem, simply because

00:00:13.678 --> 00:00:16.108
pretty much all the
mainstream recommendations

00:00:16.108 --> 00:00:19.287
for burning fat are completely outdated.

00:00:19.287 --> 00:00:21.791
In fact, look at the statistics.

00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:24.687
In America, only 2% of the population

00:00:24.687 --> 00:00:27.437
ever is successful at burning fat

00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:30.174
and achieving their weight-loss goals.

00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:34.144
An average female spends 17 years dieting,

00:00:34.144 --> 00:00:35.641
so what does that tell you?

00:00:35.641 --> 00:00:38.551
They're operating off of
incorrect information.

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:41.985
What I'm gonna tell you is based on fact,

00:00:41.985 --> 00:00:44.753
physiology books, how the body works.

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:48.253
There's two main fuel sources in the body.

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:52.252
You have fat, and you have stored sugar.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.685
There is a third one called muscle,

00:00:54.685 --> 00:00:55.717
but I'm not gonna get into that,

00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:57.030
because you have to be very, very sick

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.255
for your body to start
using muscle protein

00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:01.603
as a fuel source.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:02.972
We're going to talk
about the two main ones,

00:01:02.972 --> 00:01:04.889
which is fat and sugar.

00:01:06.029 --> 00:01:08.497
In other words, your body can store sugar,

00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:10.312
the name of that's called glycogen,

00:01:10.312 --> 00:01:11.711
in your liver and your muscles,

00:01:11.711 --> 00:01:13.746
and that can release in-between times

00:01:13.746 --> 00:01:15.722
where you're not eating

00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:18.146
or it can go up to the fat.

00:01:18.146 --> 00:01:21.118
The way it works are fat-burning hormones,

00:01:21.118 --> 00:01:23.774
based on what you eat and what you do,

00:01:23.774 --> 00:01:26.801
trigger the fat to release certain enzymes

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:30.292
to dissolve that fat,
called lipase enzymes.

00:01:30.292 --> 00:01:33.342
They're hormone-sensitive fat enzymes

00:01:33.342 --> 00:01:36.132
that break things down into ketones.

00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:39.799
Ketones are the byproduct
of fat metabolism,

00:01:40.865 --> 00:01:44.865
and your body can run on
these very efficiently.

00:01:46.222 --> 00:01:47.599
Way better, actually.

00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:49.090
It's a better fuel source.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.579
It's a cleaner fuel source.

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:51.412
Your body could run on this.

00:01:51.412 --> 00:01:53.687
Even your brain could run on ketones.

00:01:53.687 --> 00:01:55.687
Now, fat-making hormones

00:01:57.725 --> 00:01:59.554
trigger the storage of sugar

00:01:59.554 --> 00:02:03.701
and the conversion of the sugar into fat,

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.365
so that's how that works.

00:02:05.365 --> 00:02:08.987
The great majority of people are only

00:02:08.987 --> 00:02:11.654
burning sugar, which is glucose.

00:02:12.622 --> 00:02:14.622
They're not burning fat.

00:02:15.507 --> 00:02:19.418
What occurs is they will lose
some temporary water weight,

00:02:19.418 --> 00:02:22.837
and they hit a plateau
thinking that's actual fat,

00:02:22.837 --> 00:02:24.878
but they never actually burn fat.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.264
I can prove that, 'cause I
have a machine that measures

00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:28.844
how much fat someone burns,

00:02:28.844 --> 00:02:30.273
and you can very easily see

00:02:30.273 --> 00:02:33.004
they lose water weight
and then they plateau.

00:02:33.004 --> 00:02:34.651
The great majority of people burn sugar.

00:02:34.651 --> 00:02:36.567
They're not actually burning fat.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.240
In this next section,
I'm gonna tell you about

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.407
the single control factor,

00:02:42.673 --> 00:02:45.082
what determines whether you're burning fat

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:48.373
or whether you're burning sugar.

00:02:48.373 --> 00:02:51.187
So, here it is, the number one controller

00:02:51.187 --> 00:02:53.773
of whether you burn actual fat

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.656
or whether you're burning sugar

00:02:55.656 --> 00:02:58.005
is this one hormone called insulin.

00:02:58.005 --> 00:03:00.588
Insulin, even in small amounts,

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.878
has the strength and the domination

00:03:03.878 --> 00:03:07.528
to prevent you from tapping
into your fat reserve.

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:11.372
So, here's a little graph
on how much insulin,

00:03:11.372 --> 00:03:13.254
or let's just say, when
I talk about insulin,

00:03:13.254 --> 00:03:14.121
I'm gonna talk about sugar,

00:03:14.121 --> 00:03:17.172
because sugar triggers insulin.

00:03:17.172 --> 00:03:19.267
I could easily say the number one control

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:22.092
of whether you burn fat
is sugar or hidden sugars,

00:03:22.092 --> 00:03:25.612
but I'm just gonna call
insulin sugar right now.

00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:29.354
If that sugar is high, let's
say it's high sugar right here,

00:03:29.354 --> 00:03:30.604
a high insulin,

00:03:31.984 --> 00:03:33.593
you're not gonna be able to burn fat.

00:03:33.593 --> 00:03:35.143
Your body is running on sugar.

00:03:35.143 --> 00:03:39.182
So, let's say you eat moderately
and you have, let's say,

00:03:39.182 --> 00:03:40.578
half of the amount of sugar,

00:03:40.578 --> 00:03:44.642
because someone said,
"Everything in moderation."

00:03:44.642 --> 00:03:49.304
It still won't work, because
insulin has to be zero

00:03:49.304 --> 00:03:53.365
or sugar has to be zero
to tap into ketones,

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:58.214
which is the byproduct of fat
burning, which is ketosis.

00:03:58.214 --> 00:04:01.958
In other words, it's not a
graph that's a gradual graph.

00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:05.896
You have to make insulin,
or shall we say sugar,

00:04:05.896 --> 00:04:08.313
zero before you can burn fat.

00:04:09.822 --> 00:04:11.737
So now, what we're gonna talk about

00:04:11.737 --> 00:04:14.154
is this thing called ketosis.

00:04:15.132 --> 00:04:17.758
Ketosis is what we want to get into.

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:20.506
You may hear some negative
things about ketosis,

00:04:20.506 --> 00:04:22.557
because it relates to diabetes,

00:04:22.557 --> 00:04:27.292
but we're talking about doing
ketosis in a very healthy way.

00:04:27.292 --> 00:04:30.696
Ketosis is the healthiest thing to do

00:04:30.696 --> 00:04:33.185
for your blood sugars,

00:04:33.185 --> 00:04:34.435
for your heart,

00:04:36.482 --> 00:04:38.551
for your brain,

00:04:38.551 --> 00:04:42.089
and other conditions like
polycystic ovarian syndrome.

00:04:42.089 --> 00:04:44.919
Really, really important, because
think about that condition

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:47.554
the person is usually
always insulin resistant.

00:04:47.554 --> 00:04:51.854
If they go on this, they
see great improvements.

00:04:51.854 --> 00:04:54.717
So, we want to get the person in ketosis.

00:04:54.717 --> 00:04:59.630
To get in ketosis usually
does not happen overnight.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:03.506
It's easy to tap into the sugar reserve,

00:05:03.506 --> 00:05:05.094
because all you have to do is eat sugar,

00:05:05.094 --> 00:05:08.609
but to get into ketosis,
it can sometimes take

00:05:08.609 --> 00:05:10.162
way more than two days.

00:05:10.162 --> 00:05:13.734
It could take a week to
two weeks up to a month

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:18.662
and maybe, in some situations,
five or even six weeks

00:05:18.662 --> 00:05:20.997
before you're really
hardcore into fat burning.

00:05:20.997 --> 00:05:22.816
Now, why is that?

00:05:22.816 --> 00:05:25.963
Because you've been living
on sugar your whole life,

00:05:25.963 --> 00:05:28.708
and your system is so inefficient

00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:32.448
and so used to burning
sugar to convert that over.

00:05:32.448 --> 00:05:34.276
It's called a keto adaptation,

00:05:34.276 --> 00:05:36.746
so you're adapting to burning fat.

00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:38.356
It just takes a little bit longer.

00:05:38.356 --> 00:05:39.571
Don't worry about it,

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:41.318
because you can see ketones in your urine

00:05:41.318 --> 00:05:43.268
within a few days, but the point is

00:05:43.268 --> 00:05:45.295
you want to stick with it a little longer.

00:05:45.295 --> 00:05:47.396
I think what discourages a lot of people

00:05:47.396 --> 00:05:51.052
is they think they're gonna
burn fat in a day or two,

00:05:51.052 --> 00:05:52.980
and they get discouraged and they stop.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.253
When, in fact, to adapt
your body into fat burning,

00:05:56.253 --> 00:05:58.906
it could take up to a
month to possibly six weeks

00:05:58.906 --> 00:06:00.853
in very extreme cases.

00:06:00.853 --> 00:06:03.941
I'm telling you that because
it might happen in a week

00:06:03.941 --> 00:06:05.728
or maybe a little longer than a week,

00:06:05.728 --> 00:06:08.519
but just hang in there and stick with it,

00:06:08.519 --> 00:06:10.203
because it will happen.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.548
Your body will be burning fat,

00:06:11.548 --> 00:06:14.158
and a lot of problems
will actually go away.

00:06:14.158 --> 00:06:18.125
Now, let's talk about what
foods that you have to eat

00:06:18.125 --> 00:06:19.792
to get into ketosis.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.449
So, here's what you need to eat.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:26.669
Number one, you want to
keep your carbohydrates

00:06:26.669 --> 00:06:30.267
within 5 to 10% of the entire amount of

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.679
calories that you eat in a given day.

00:06:32.679 --> 00:06:35.467
Now, the type of carbohydrates
we're gonna recommend

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:38.240
are vegetable in nature.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.146
So, why vegetable?

00:06:40.146 --> 00:06:42.970
Even though they have a
small amount of carbohydrate,

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.447
they have a lot of vitamins and minerals

00:06:45.447 --> 00:06:49.565
that you're not gonna
get with protein or fat,

00:06:49.565 --> 00:06:52.935
so we do want the vegetable
carbohydrates here

00:06:52.935 --> 00:06:54.745
in a good amount.

00:06:54.745 --> 00:06:56.130
The net sugars from that is gonna be

00:06:56.130 --> 00:07:00.373
very, very, very low, if anything at all.

00:07:00.373 --> 00:07:04.731
25% of your diet should
come in the form of protein.

00:07:04.731 --> 00:07:07.192
This thing that I'm telling
you is not the Atkins diet.

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:10.192
Atkins is a lot of protein.

00:07:10.192 --> 00:07:13.292
Our body is not made
out of a carbohydrate.

00:07:13.292 --> 00:07:16.380
Some of our body is protein,

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.443
but a lot of our body is made out of fat,

00:07:18.443 --> 00:07:20.317
and that's the third one right here.

00:07:20.317 --> 00:07:22.900
65 to 80% of your calories

00:07:24.184 --> 00:07:25.989
should be in the form of fat.

00:07:25.989 --> 00:07:29.699
Now, before you freak out, realize that

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:33.310
I'm actually have been in
